e, Canal de Cuemanco, Xochimilco"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/158482"} "27 from 13 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The favorites for the double sculls event at the 1968 Summer Olympics were Switzerland’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/39703"} "Melchior Bürgin"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/39824"} "Martin Studach"] ". Together they had won the last two editions of the European Championships, the most recent World Championships, and the 1965 and 1967 Double Sculls Challenge Cups at the Henley Royal Regatta. Among their challengers would be " [:a {:href "/athletes/40358"} "Anatoly Sass"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/40383"} "Aleksandr Timoshinin"] " of the Soviet Union, the nation defending its Olympic title, Bulgaria’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/35993"} "Atanas Zhelev"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/36001"} "Yordan Valchev"] ", the most recent European runners-up, and " [:a {:href "/athletes/39980"} "Jaroslav Hellebrand"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/40011"} "Petr Krátký"] " of Czechoslovakia, who had won bronze medals at the last two European Championships."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In the opening round it was the Bulgarians who posted the fastest time, but most attention was focused on the Swiss duo, as Studach overexerted himself in Mexico City’s high altitude and collapsed, leading to his hospitalization and replacement by " [:a {:href "/athletes/39790"} "Hans Ruckstuhl"] ". The Swiss, along with Czechoslovakia among others, were subsequently eliminated in the semi-finals. In the final, the relatively unheralded Dutch duo of " [:a {:href "/athletes/39010"} "Leendert van Dis"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/38887"} "Harry Droog"] " led the race most of the way, but were passed by Sass and Timoshinin in the last 500 metres and forced to settle for silver. Americans " [:a {:href "/athletes/40766"} "Bill Maher"] " and " [:a {:href ""} "John Nunn"] ", a silver medalist at the 1967 Pan American Games, finished well ahead of the Bulgarians to take bronze."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Pair"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/40358"} "Anatoly Sass"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/40383"} "Aleksandr Timoshinin"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/URS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/URS.png"}] "URS"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/39010"} "Leendert van Dis"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/38887"} "Harry Droog"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/NED"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/NED.png"}] "NED"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/40766"} "Bill Maher"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/40820"} "John Nunn"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/35993"} "Atanas Zhelev"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/36001"} "Yordan Valchev"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/BUL"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/BUL.png"}] "BUL"]] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "5"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/37648"} "Uli Schmied"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/37615"} "Manfred Haake"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GDR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/